  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want a tap on a member's avatar in a topic to offer Profil, Envoyer un MP, Ajouter à la whitelist / blacklist, and so on, as the legacy app does. When the member has no avatar, I want a default one rather than nothing. Operator report after a device test, 2026-11-07. **M4**.\n\n### Report\n- A tap on the avatar should open the member menu: profile, MP, whitelist, blacklist, and so on (see legacy).\n- A default avatar should show when there is none. The operator suggests a generic silhouette in the style of the classic default profile picture. It must be original art: no real person's photo or likeness.\n\n### To analyse (read-only, before any fix)\n- Legacy @ 2440d79: the avatar or pseudo tap menu in `MessagesView.swift` and the reader JS bridge.\n- SwiftHFR today:\n  - the avatar `<img class=\"avatar\">` in `TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:136-137`;\n  - the profile screen (LOT-116, #207);\n  - the blacklist and whitelist (LOT-118, #209, M4, not done);\n  - MP compose (LOT-128).\n- The default avatar in the reader HTML: a local SVG served through the `hfrreader:` scheme, under the CSP. Make it consistent with #569's monogram.",
