   "body": "## Analysis (read-only, sub-orch) 2026-11-07\n\nRead from `origin/dev-swift` @ `4b1e77f`; legacy @ `2440d79`.\n\n### SwiftHFR today: why a tap on the avatar does nothing\n- **Avatar markup.** `TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:136-138` writes `<img class=\"avatar\">` only when `avatarURL` exists. With no avatar there is nothing, and the header starts with the pseudo.\n- **The avatar is inert on purpose.** LOT-087 spec, intentional difference 5: \"the author menu opens from the pseudo (a button); legacy opened it from the avatar image, which stays inert here\".\n- **The pseudo is not tappable either.**\n  - The pseudo becomes `<button class=\"menu-author\" data-menu=\"avatar\">` only when `showsAuthorMenus` is on (`TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:140-146`).\n  - That flag is `registry.offers(.avatar)` (`TopicReaderModel+Menu.swift:43`), which needs a handler for `.profile`, `.privateMessage`, `.blocklist` or `.allowlist` (`MessageActionRegistry.swift:290-296`).\n  - `TopicReaderView.installMenuActions` (`:247-266`) registers none of them. So the pseudo is a plain `<span>` and **no author menu exists at all**.\n- **A blocked or failed avatar is removed.** `reader.js:16` (failed or blocked) and `:33` (tap-to-load mode) call `img.remove()` on `.avatar`, so the header loses it with no fallback.\n- **The policy is already ported.** `MessageMenuPolicy.authorActions` (`MessageMenuAction.swift:231-240`) gives Profil when `profileURL`; MP when not own and `privateMessageURL`; Blacklist and Whitelist when not own and the pseudo is non-empty. This matches legacy `MessagesView.swift:205-217`.\n\n### Legacy @ 2440d79\n- **Tap targets.** `templatev2.htm:4-5`: both the avatar `div.left2` and the pseudo `div.left` call `touchHeaderMessage(this,'avatar')`.\n- **Routing.** `MessagesView.swift:1525-1536` `presentPopupMenu` routes source `.avatar` to `onPopupAvatarSheetRequest` → `presentAvatarActionSheet` `:3610-3616`:\n  - **With a profile URL**, it opens the **profile screen directly**, with quick actions MP / Blacklist / Whitelist (`userProfileQuickActions` `:3582-3608`; BL/WL toggles `:3652-3698` via `ObjCProfileFilterListManager`, then a reload).\n  - **Without one**, it opens `MessageAvatarActionSheetView` (`:5307-5393`): an avatar preview, then Profil, MP, Whitelist, Blacklist (destructive).\n- **Default avatar.**\n  - Reader: CSS `--imagefile-avatar` → `avatar_male_gray_on_{light,dark}_48x48.png` (`MessagesView.swift:2411`, `style-liste.css:31,195`), with the class `noavatar` (`LinkItem.m:65-69`).\n  - Sheet: the same PNG (`:5429`), or `person.crop.circle.fill`.\n\n### Entries and their dependencies\n| Entry | Can ship now? | How |\n|---|---|---|\n| Profil | **yes** (LOT-116 #207 closed) | `profileURL` is `/hfr/profil-<id>.htm` (`MessageActionsParser.swift:37,159`) → `HFRLinkRoute.route` `.profile(memberID)` → `UserProfileModel`, exactly as the link path does (`TopicReaderView.swift:278`); fetched without cookies |\n| MP | **yes** (LOT-128 #219 closed) | `privateMessageURL` is `/message.php?…cat=prive&dest=…` (`MessageActionsParser.swift:90-94`) → `NewMessageTarget(link:)` (`ReplyPosting.swift:26-44`, `R45b`) → `ReplyComposerModel(composing: .newPrivateMessage)`, as `MessageListView.swift:54` does. Needs a composer (logged in). UXD-20 already says \"the recipient stays one, from a message\": this handler is the missing reader-side entry |\n| Blacklist / Whitelist | **no**: LOT-118 #209 (`status: ready`, M4) owns the writes | The store exists (`PseudoListsSnapshot.liveStore`, read-only here). LOT-118 should register two `MessageActionHandler`s (the toggle, then `applyDisplaySettings()` to re-render, like legacy's reload). Per the registry design, nothing else changes |\n\n### Default avatar under the CSP\n- **Not an `<img src>`.** `reader.js:196-200` sends every `img[src]` through policy C, and an `hfrreader:` source is not an HFR image, so it would be replaced or removed.\n- **Option A, inline SVG in the header** (recommended). The builder writes a fixed `<svg class=\"avatar avatar-default\" viewBox=\"0 0 32 32\" aria-hidden=\"true\">` with two shapes: a circle for the head and a rounded path for the shoulders, `fill: var(--secondary)` on a `var(--quaternary)`-style disc.\n  - No request, and nothing for the CSP to allow (no script, no external reference).\n  - It is original geometric art, not a likeness of anyone, and does not copy legacy's PNG.\n- **Option B, `hfrreader://resource/avatar-default.svg` as a CSS `background-image`** (allowed by `img-src hfrreader:`). It needs a second case in `ReaderWebController.start` `:260-262`, which only serves `/reader.css` today. An SVG served this way cannot follow the theme colours, so A is simpler.\n- **`reader.js:16,33`.** Swap the avatar for the same placeholder instead of `remove()`, so a blocked, failed or tap-mode avatar still leaves something to tap.\n- **Consistency with #569.**\n  - #569 proposes a **monogram** (initials on a hashed colour) for the MP list.\n  - This issue asks for a **silhouette**.\n  - **Operator decision needed:** one placeholder for both screens. Either the silhouette everywhere (the reader SVG and `MessageAvatarView.placeholder` built from the same path), or the monogram everywhere (the reader renders the initials as text in a `<span>`, with a palette class index computed in Swift from the same stable hash).\n  - Whichever is chosen, put the shape or hash in one shared helper and record one GAP row.\n\n### Proposed fix\n1. **Tap targets.** Make the avatar (real or default) and the pseudo one `<button data-menu=\"avatar\">`, or two buttons with the same `data-*`. Revise LOT-087 difference 5: the avatar is tappable again, and the placeholder means \"missing avatar\" never leaves no way in.\n2. **Handlers.** Register `ProfileActionHandler` and `PrivateMessageActionHandler` in `installMenuActions`; MP only with a composer.\n3. **Menu or profile first.** Use the anchored author menu from #594 (Profil, MP, and later BL/WL), not legacy's profile-first jump: the operator asks for a menu. Record this as a UX difference (GAP row; optionally quick actions in `UserProfileView` later, GAP-167).\n4. **Default avatar.** Option A, plus the `reader.js` swap.\n5. **Tests.**\n   - Builder output with and without `avatarURL`, and with a blocked author.\n   - Registry `offers(.avatar)` becomes true.\n   - Profile route from `profileURL`; `NewMessageTarget` from `privateMessageURL`, nil for a non-forum or non-`prive` link.\n   - App-hosted web test: a tap on the avatar posts `menu`/`avatar`; a blocked avatar keeps its placeholder.\n\n### Scope, effort, routing, conflicts\n- **Effort.** Medium (one session plus a Mac check in light, dark, Increase Contrast and Dynamic Type XL).\n- **Routing.** Sonnet 5.5 → Opus 5.5 review. BL/WL stay with LOT-118 (Sonnet → Opus).\n- **Dependencies.** #594 (anchored menu, same bridge message) should land first. The placeholder choice is shared with #569.\n- **Conflicts.**\n  - **#575** edits `ReaderWebController.swift` and `TopicReaderView.swift`: rebase after it. Option A avoids touching `ReaderWebController.start`.\n  - **#583** is toolbar-only: low risk.\n  - **#594** touches the same `reader.js` click handler and `installMenuActions`: sequence #594 → #595.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
